This directory is intentionally empty, and intentionally present.

ferrum.secretsDir points here for the example host, and several checks in
nix/modules/flake/checks.nix resolve this path at evaluation time, so the
directory has to exist in a fresh clone even though it holds nothing. Git
does not track empty directories, which is what this file is for.

It holds nothing because an example must not ship secrets. It previously
carried three sops-encrypted servarr API keys, encrypted to an age
recipient nobody cloning this repository has, and which by existing
without their -raw counterparts tripped an assertion in every one of the
three servarr modules. Deleting them is the remedy those assertions
themselves recommend.

Secrets are generated on the host by ferrum-apply, or written through the
dashboard. Neither belongs in a template someone copies.
